## Goal
- Complete autonomous Measure workflow: finish WebTorrent Download Management track, Legacy Test Audit track, and make progress on TypeScript Strictness Re-enablement track.

## Constraints & Preferences
- Follow measure/autonomous_prompt.md: TDD, commit after each phase, verify with tests + build + smoke test
- Keep tech-debt.md and lessons-learned.md at ≤50 lines
- Archive completed tracks to measure/archive/

## Progress
### Done
- **WebTorrent Download Management** (3 phases): Backend torrent routes (25 tests), enhanced ActivityQueuePage with sort/filter/search/SSE/priority controls, priority API integration, app build clean, 1800 tests green — archived
- **Legacy Test Audit** (3 phases): Audited 340 backup tests in app_src_backup, determined all obsolete (110 duplicates, 150 test removed code, 95 outdated), deleted all, 1800 tests green — archived
- Updated current_directive.md twice; added lessons-learned entry about enhancing existing pages vs creating new ones

### In Progress
- **TypeScript Strictness Re-enablement** (server workspace): Enabled `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` and `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` in server/tsconfig.json. Fixing 865 type errors by adding `| undefined` to optional interface properties. Fixed contracts.ts (ParsedPaginationParams) and errors.ts (ErrorEnvelope). App workspace already clean (0 errors).

### Blocked
- (none)

## Key Decisions
- Enhanced existing ActivityQueuePage instead of creating separate DownloadList/TorrentRow components — faster and more maintainable; existing DataTable and API patterns reused
- Deleted all 340 backup tests rather than restoring any — audit determined active test suite already covers all functional areas; backup tests use old APIs/patterns
- Fixing exactOptionalPropertyTypes errors by updating interface definitions (`prop?: T` → `prop?: T | undefined`) rather than call sites — fixes multiple errors per change

## Next Steps
1. Continue fixing server type errors: update remaining interface definitions with `| undefined`
2. Run `tsc --noEmit` to verify error count reduction
3. Run full test suite (`CI=true npm test`) to confirm no regressions
4. Commit progress and update plan.md
5. If error count remains high, consider splitting into sub-tracks per module

